From 6aa2fa634b8b9606129878b226d17e88b2ed893c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Petr=20=C5=A0tetiar?= <petr.stetiar@prplfoundation.org>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 21:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Plugin: do not save the MLD info of a link socket running in
 another MLD than the link's unit is configured with
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

wifiGen_mld_fetchSockLinkSSID() maps a hostapd control socket to its SSID
for the wpactrl manager (wld_wpaCtrlMngr_checkAllIfaces() ->
fFetchSockLinkIface, src/nl80211/wld_wpaCtrlMngr.c) and, on the way,
saves the MLD info carried by the socket name into that SSID when the
socket belongs to the manager's radio and the SSID is configured with a
link id other than the running one: the running link id, the PRIMARY
role when the socket's MLD netdev is the SSID's own interface name
(which makes the link the primary link of its MLD unit,
wld_ssid_setMLDRole() -> wld_mld_setPrimaryLink()), and in that case a
reset of the link id of every neighbour link running in another MLD
netdev.

That takes a running BSS as proof that the desired MLD config of the
link has been applied. It has not when the link was just moved to
another MLD unit: s_checkMLDUnit() (src/wld_ssid.c) moves the link
object to the target unit at once, the FSM marks it configured before
any teardown (s_checkApDependency() -> wld_mld_saveLinkConfigured(),
"configured" meaning being/been configured by the FSM), and the BSS
added for the previous unit stays loaded in hostapd until
GEN_FSM_REMOVE_LINK / GEN_FSM_REMOVE_HOSTAPD tear it down. Every socket
scan in between adopts the old BSS into the new unit.

Observed on a mac80211 AP MLD setup during Freedom 102-apmld_step_2.t
(AP1 = wlan2.1, 2.4 GHz; private MLD wlan1.1 with the 5/6 GHz links 1/2
and AP1 as link 3). SSID.1.MLDUnit 0 -> 12 makes AP1 a single-link MLD
wlan2.1 (socket wlan2.1_link0); MLDUnit 12 -> 0 then gives:

  mld: reset primary link DEFAULT_RADIO0 (s_takeLink)     <- unit 12 emptied
  genFsm: wlan2.1: target is main AP, schedule re-add config
  ssid: DEFAULT_RADIO1: ssid has no mld link id           <- 5 GHz link
  ssid: DEFAULT_RADIO2: ssid has no mld link id           <- 6 GHz link
  hostapd: Remove interface 'wlan2.1_link0'
  hostapd: Configuration file: /tmp/wlan2_hapd.conf (phy wlan2) --> new PHY
  nlApi: link:Id(0) in mld iface(ifName:wlan2.1) (ifId:18) nLinks(1)

The socket refresh run by wld_rad_hostapd_removeConf() before the
removal (patch "nl80211: remove the other loaded hostapd ifaces before
the main iface on a radio re-add") maps the still running wlan2.1_link0
by its link MAC to AP1, already registered in unit 0 and configured
with link id -1, and adopts it: AP1 becomes the primary link of unit 0
and the 5/6 GHz links lose their link ids because they run in wlan1.1.
The radio removal only resets the link ids of the radio's own APs
(wld_rad_resetApMldLinks()), not the primary pointer, and the config
written after it follows the configured primary
(wifiGen_mld_selectPrimLinkSSID() via wld_hostapd_ap_selectApLinkIface()):
interface=wlan2.1, mld_addr=<AP1 MAC>. hostapd groups AP MLD links by
that interface name (hostapd_bss_setup_multi_link(), src/ap/hostapd.c,
strcmp of conf->iface with mld->name; mld_addr is not compared), so it
creates a new MLD wlan2.1 instead of adding AP1 to wlan1.1: the private
MLD is split, APMLD.MLDMACAddress switches to AP1's MAC and the test
finds a single link. The same round trip in a run where AP1 was not the
running main VAP of its radio took the secondary BSS removal, which has
no scan before the removal, and joined wlan1.1.

The refresh before the removal is not the defect, it only makes it
deterministic: the same adoption runs from every other socket scan (the
wpactrl connect timer, s_syncOnRadUp() and s_ifaceCreated() in
src/Plugin/wifiGen_eventHandlers.c and src/Plugin/wifiGen_fsm.c) and
adopts the same stale BSS when one of them runs between the MLDUnit
change and the teardown.

Fix: save the MLD info of a link socket only when the socket's MLD
netdev is the one the link's MLD unit is configured with. hostapd names
the MLD after the "interface=" line of the config the BSS was added
with, i.e. after the primary link selected when that config was
written, and wifiGen_mld_selectPrimLinkSSID() always selects the unit's
configured primary link when there is one. A running link socket whose
MLD netdev differs from the interface name of the unit's configured
primary link is therefore that of a BSS added for a previous MLD
configuration of the link (such as its previous unit), still loaded in
hostapd. Its SSID is still returned, so the socket is still mapped to
its wpactrl interface and the BSS is removed exactly as before; only its
link id, role, the primary pointer and the neighbours' link ids are left
alone, and a warning names the two ifaces. When the unit has no
configured primary link (first setup, or the primary link just left the
unit) the running MLD defines it, as before.

With that, unit 0 keeps wlan1.1 as primary link over the move-back, the
regenerated radio config carries interface=wlan1.1 and
mld_addr=<wlan1.1 MAC> for AP1, and hostapd adds AP1 as a link of the
existing MLD wlan1.1.

Signed-off-by: Petr Štetiar <petr.stetiar@prplfoundation.org>
---
 src/Plugin/wifiGen_mld.c | 39 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 39 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/Plugin/wifiGen_mld.c b/src/Plugin/wifiGen_mld.c
index 6e25c2988934..68714949f8de 100644
--- a/src/Plugin/wifiGen_mld.c
+++ b/src/Plugin/wifiGen_mld.c
@@ -165,6 +165,34 @@ static T_SSID* s_fetchLinkSSID(const char* mldIface, int32_t linkId, const char*
     return pSSID;
 }
 
+/**
+ * @brief check whether a running BSS socket is of the MLD its link is configured with
+ *
+ * The MLD netdev of a running link socket ("<mldIface>_link<N>") is the
+ * interface name hostapd groups the MLD by: the "interface=" line of the
+ * config the BSS was added with, i.e. the interface name of the primary link
+ * selected when that config was written. The MLD pWHM configures the link
+ * with is its MLD unit, whose configured primary link
+ * (wifiGen_mld_selectPrimLinkSSID()) names the netdev every config of the
+ * unit is written with. When the two differ, the socket is of a BSS added
+ * for a previous MLD configuration of the link (e.g. its previous MLD unit,
+ * after an MLDUnit change) which is still loaded in hostapd, so its MLD
+ * info must not be saved into the link's current unit.
+ *
+ * @param pLinkSSID ssid of the link mapped to the socket
+ * @param mldIface MLD netdev of the socket
+ *
+ * @return true when the MLD info of the socket applies to the link's MLD unit
+ *         (also when the unit has no configured primary link yet)
+ */
+static bool s_isSockOfConfiguredMld(T_SSID* pLinkSSID, const char* mldIface) {
+    wld_mldLink_t* pPrimLink = wld_mld_getPrimaryLink(pLinkSSID->pMldLink);
+    if((pPrimLink == NULL) || !wld_mld_isLinkConfigured(pPrimLink)) {
+        return true;
+    }
+    return swl_str_matches(wld_mld_getLinkIfName(pPrimLink), mldIface);
+}
+
 T_SSID* wifiGen_mld_fetchSockLinkSSID(wld_wpaCtrlMngr_t* pMgr, const char* sockName) {
     ASSERT_STR(sockName, NULL, ME, "empty socket name");
     const char* refIface = wld_wpaCtrlInterface_getName(wld_wpaCtrlMngr_getFirstInterface(pMgr));
@@ -184,6 +212,17 @@ T_SSID* wifiGen_mld_fetchSockLinkSSID(wld_wpaCtrlMngr_t* pMgr, const char* sockN
     T_SSID* pLinkSSID = s_fetchLinkSSID(mldIface, linkId, sockName);
     ASSERTS_NOT_NULL(pLinkSSID, NULL, ME, "sock(%s): Fail to match any SSID", sockName);
 
+    /*
+     * A socket of a BSS still running in another MLD than the one the link's
+     * unit is configured with (e.g. the BSS of its previous unit, pending
+     * removal) is only mapped: its MLD info is not that of the link's unit.
+     */
+    if(!s_isSockOfConfiguredMld(pLinkSSID, mldIface)) {
+        SAH_TRACEZ_WARNING(ME, "%s: sock(%s) runs in mld iface(%s) but mld unit(%d) is configured with primary link iface(%s): skip saving its MLD info",
+                           pLinkSSID->Name, sockName, mldIface, pLinkSSID->mldUnit, wld_mld_getPrimaryLinkIfName(pLinkSSID->pMldLink));
+        return pLinkSSID;
+    }
+
     /*
      * update SSID MLD info of fetched wpactrl sock, when:
      * 0) sock belongs the current wpactrl mngr (ie same SSID's radio)
